      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1873, Glenwood boasted a woolen factory, flour mill, foundry, machine shop, and wagon factory, fueling early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name appears in both the FIPS‑55 and GNIS databases, confirming its official recognition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/mo/glenwood-xx-schuyler-profile.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glenwood’s rapid expansion came from its position at the junction of the St. Louis, Kansas City & Nebraska Railroad and the Keokuk & Western railway.",
